      en: ["Named after the historic Lyssons sugar plantation that dominated the area in the 1800s.", "Located approximately 3 kilometers east of the historic town of Morant Bay.", "Was a strategic point on the route taken by Paul Bogle's followers during the 1865 Rebellion.", "The facility was fully renovated and modernized in 2015 by the Tourism Enhancement Fund.", "The beach is protected by an offshore reef, resulting in exceptionally calm and safe waters.", "Features modern amenities including picnic areas, gazebos, and accessible walkways.", "Historically used as a shipping point for raw sugar produced in the St. Thomas interior.", "The park is a major venue for local seafood festivals and national holiday celebrations."],
